{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9833","id":4763426868,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLj5faM8AAAABG-wgNA","html_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9833","diff_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9833.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9833.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/9833","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9833/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9833/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/9833/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/statuses/1247132fa147f82a14e36757d437ba1507a629b1","number":9833,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[grug] Compute the MoE routing-weight gradient on the expert side","user":{"login":"mcwitt","id":319411,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxOTQxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/319411?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt","html_url":"https://github.com/mcwitt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`moe_mlp` and `MoEExpertMlp` gain `routing_weight_gradient`, which selects how the ragged all-to-all backend differentiates the combine weights. The default, `EXACT`, keeps the expert outputs for the backward and differentiates the combine. `EXPERT_SIDE` takes the gradient from the expert MLP's own backward and skips storing and returning the outputs. The hero selects `EXPERT_SIDE`; other ragged users keep `EXACT`, and other implementations reject `EXPERT_SIDE`.\n\nThe gradient with respect to the combine weight w[t,k] is dS[t,k] = <dout[t], y[t,k]>, and it was the only backward consumer of the expert down projection's output y. Since dy = w * dout and dh = dy W2^T, the same value is rowsum(dh * h) / w, built from tensors the expert MLP backward already holds. One custom VJP from dispatch to combine now returns s = <h, dh> per expert row, which XLA fuses into the SwiGLU backward's elementwise pass, sends it back with one [C, 1] f32 all-to-all per chunk, and forms dS = s / w in f32. Dropped and padded slots get 0 by selection, not division. Where w * dout rounds to zero in the cotangent dtype (a zero weight, or in float16 a normal weight times a small cotangent), the row's cotangent carries nothing and dS comes out zero or inexact. The hero's routing weights are positive renormalized sigmoids and its cotangents bf16, which has fp32's exponent range.\n\nThe hero runs its routed experts at a latent width, with a down projection before routing and an up projection after. With y unneeded, the hero's `offload_carry` remat policy saves the routed output before the up projection (18 GiB across 48 layers), and the recompute drops the expert down GEMM, the return all-to-all and the combine gather-sum. The backward's transports reuse the forward transfers' send and receive offsets, swapped, instead of exchanging offsets in another collective (carried over from the closed #9481). On GPU, the backward's weighted output cotangents come from #9832's dispatch scatter kernel, which reads each token's cotangent row once.\n\nThe carry offload therefore defaults to a 0.78 memory fraction and an XLA memory-limit slop factor of 105, the percentage of the memory budget that the scheduler and remat plan against. At 0.75 and 85 that budget (87.7 GiB) is below the backward's ~105 GiB, and XLA would recompute the saved output; 0.78 and 105 give 114 GiB. With the backward's transports no longer ordered after the recompute's, more than one collective in flight gave run-to-run different gradients or hung on GB200, so every ragged run now forces an overlap limit of 1. Without the carry offload, where the latency-hiding scheduler is off and the limit does not bind, #9831 already runs collectives synchronously.\n\nForward, dx, dW13 and dW2 are bitwise unchanged; with `EXPERT_SIDE`, dS differs at bf16 rounding (median ~1 ulp) at nonzero weights. Peak HBM rises by ~20 GiB to ~125 GiB of the 143.75 GiB pool. In #9708's series (one 64-GPU hero rack, restore step-180000, seed 0, 100 steps), the step fell from 13.542 to 13.130 s (+3.14%) on a base with #9831's remat flag and #9832's unfilled buffers.\n\nSplit from #9708. Part of #9636.\n","labels":[{"id":10166074947,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLj5faM8AAAACXfH-Qw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/labels/agent-generated","name":"agent-generated","description":"Created by automation/agent","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11981276996,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLj5faM8AAAACyiPHRA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/labels/agentic-lint","name":"agentic-lint","description":"Local agentic lint review completed","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-06T19:07:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T19:11:11Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a7b95c1384fc14f2dd1ce3e92e75326d26ddd4f0","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dlwh","id":9633,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2MzM=","avatar_url":"http